[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    recomputed every iteration at `-O0`). Whenever the bound is `<= 0` the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    function silently performs no work — this is the only way the C "rejects" an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    input. The bound is computed with wrapping 32-bit arithmetic:
