[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mVerification is complete. The C library is one function ([38;5;10mpremultiply[0m, 20 lines), and the Rust translation was already structurally faithful — but it had two real divergences on the error path.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Divergences found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both were in how the Rust read the [38;5;10mcp_image_t[0m header fields, and both reproduced [1monly under the debug cdylib[22m — the release build happened to match, so a release-only run would have wrongly declared the translation correct.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
| Trigger | C | Rust (before) | Cause |[0m[0m
|---|---|---|---|[0m[0m
| [38;5;10mimg == NULL[0m | SIGSEGV (11) | SIGABRT (6) | [38;5;10m(*img).w[0m emits rustc's debug [38;5;10mub_checks[0m null/alignment assertion; the panic can't unwind across [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m so it aborts |[0m[0m
| misaligned [38;5;10mimg[0m | succeeds (plain [38;5;10mmov[0m) | SIGABRT | first fix used [38;5;10mptr::read_volatile[0m, which carries a debug [3malignment[23m precondition. [38;5;10mread_unaligned[0m was no good either — it carries a [3mnon-null[23m precondition, re-breaking case 1 |[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix reads the fields one [38;5;10mu8[0m at a time via [38;5;10mread_volatile[0m: alignment 1 is satisfied by every address and a [38;5;10mu8[0m volatile read performs no null check, so both cases now match the C exactly. The pixel-data loop was left on plain derefs, since [38;5;10mu8[0m alignment is trivial and the null check is unreachable (each iteration touches [38;5;10mdata[i+3][0m first, so a null [38;5;10mpix[0m faults at address 3 in both).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Ground truth used[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I disassembled the C [38;5;10m.so[0m rather than inferring from the source, which pinned down the semantics the tests assert: [38;5;10mstride[0m is a wrapping 32-bit [38;5;10mw * 4[0m ([38;5;10mcltq; shl $2,%eax[0m), the loop bound is a wrapping 32-bit signed [38;5;10mimul[0m with a [38;5;10mjl[0m compare, and the output conversion is [38;5;10mcvttss2si[0m plus a low-byte store. Two negative dimensions therefore produce a [3mpositive[23m bound and the loop runs — preserved, not "fixed".[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Coverage[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **[38;5;10mSYMBOLS.md[0m** — C exports exactly one symbol; [38;5;10mnm -D[0m diff is empty for both cdylib profiles, and the Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m imports nothing outside libc/libgcc-unwind.[0m[0m
- **[38;5;10mCONFIGS.md[0m** — 28 rows, all passing. Includes an exhaustive sweep of all 256 channel values × 256 alphas (both uniform and distinct-channel), shape-equivalence across 8 [38;5;10m(w,h)[0m pairs with the same product, misaligned pixel buffers, and 20 000-iteration seeded fuzz.[0m[0m
